  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_7' aria-label=\" Vishvjeet and Others versus State of Uttar Pradesh and Another pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('7','2026','2026_4_184_190','2026INSC254'); ><font size='4'> <strong>VISHVJEET AND OTHERS<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>STATE OF UTTAR PRADESH AND ANOTHER </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 4 S.C.R. 184</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 254</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000992026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : VIKRAM NATH, SANDEEP MEHTA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Matter pertained to acts of hooliganism by the Barabanki Bar Members by attacking advocate representing petitioners in toll plaza case. Headnotes&dagger; Constitution of India &ndash; Article 32 &ndash; Conduct of law professionals &ndash; Acts of hooliganism &ndash; for toll collection duty at the Toll Plaza on Lucknow-Sultanpur Highway, in District Barabanki, Uttar Pradesh &ndash; Advocate-complainant allegedly refused to pay requisite toll charges while passing through the toll plaza, and a verbal spat and scuffle ensued between the advocate and the staff<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 17-03-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> WRIT PETITION (CRIMINAL) No. 109/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Disposed off</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('7','2026','2026_4_184_190','2026INSC254','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitvie